    "# QuantumLens: Explainable Text Summarization and KNN-Based Document Clustering\n",
    "## Course: Advanced Social Media and Text Analysis\n",
    "### System Architecture, Extractive NLP, Graph-Theoretic Clustering, and Evidence-Based Attribution\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "### Executive Summary & Academic Scope\n",
    "**QuantumLens** is an end-to-end natural language processing (NLP) and machine learning framework designed for unsupervised document summarization, graph-based clustering, and transparent cluster assignment explanations. While the primary demonstration corpus explores **Quantum Computing Latest News** (spanning superconducting qubits, neutral atoms, trapped ions, error correction, algorithms, post-quantum cryptography, commercial applications, and classical HPC baselines), the system architecture is domain-agnostic and fully capable of ingesting, preprocessing, summarizing, and clustering documents from arbitrary text domains.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Core System Architecture\n",
    "```\n",
    " +-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n",
    " |                      Phase 1: Multi-Modal Ingestion & Validation                   |\n",
    " |  - Direct Text  - Multi-File .txt  - CSV Ingestion  - Schema & Deduplication Check|\n",
    " +-----------------------------------------+-----------------------------------------+\n",
    "                                           |\n",
    "                                           v\n",
    " +-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n",
    " |                     Phase 2: Transparent NLP Preprocessing                        |\n",
    " |  - Raw Text Preservation (for Summarization)                                      |\n",
    " |  - HTML Removal -> Tokenization -> Stopword Pruning -> Domain-Aware Lemmatization |\n",
    " +-----------------------------------------+-----------------------------------------+\n",
    "                                           |\n",
    "                     +---------------------+---------------------+\n",
    "                     |                                           |\n",
    "                     v                                           v\n",
    " +---------------------------------------+   +---------------------------------------+\n",
    " |  Phase 3: Extractive Summarization   |   |   Phase 4: Vector Space Modeling      |\n",
    " |  - Sentence Tokenization              |   |  - TF-IDF (Unigrams & Bigrams)        |\n",
    " |  - Sentence-Sentence Cosine Graph     |   |  - Sublinear Term-Frequency Scaling   |\n",
    " |  - TextRank (PageRank Centrality)     |   |  - Optional Semantic Embeddings       |\n",
    " |  - Chronological Order & Compression  |   +-------------------+-------------------+\n",
    " +-------------------+-------------------+                       |\n",
    "                     |                                           |\n",
    "                     |       +-----------------------------------+\n",
    "                     |       |\n",
    "                     v       v\n",
    " +-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n",
    " |                     Phase 5: KNN-Based Graph Clustering                           |\n",
    " |  - Scikit-Learn NearestNeighbors (Metric = Cosine Distance)                       |\n",
    " |  - Distance Inversion: Similarity s = 1 - d                                       |\n",
    " |  - Thresholded Undirected Similarity Graph G = (V, E) with tau cutoff             |\n",
    " |  - Connected Components -> Graph Clusters                                         |\n",
    " |  - Degree-0 Node Isolation -> Cluster -1 (Outliers)                               |\n",
    " +-----------------------------------------+-----------------------------------------+\n",
    "                                           |\n",
    "                     +---------------------+---------------------+\n",
    "                     |                                           |\n",
    "                     v                                           v\n",
    " +---------------------------------------+   +---------------------------------------+\n",
    " | Phase 6: Explainability Engine        |   | Phase 7: Cluster Synthesis            |\n",
    " |  - Document vs Cluster Top Keywords   |   |  - Graph Centrality Exemplar / Medoid |\n",
    " |  - Shared Feature Overlap             |   |  - Cluster-Level Thematic Synthesis   |\n",
    " |  - Nearest Neighbor Links & Weights   |   |  - Intra-Cluster Subtopic Divergence  |\n",
    " |  - Graph Path Tracing (Chaining Check)|   +-------------------+-------------------+\n",
    " |  - Alternative Cluster & Margin Delta |                       |\n",
    " |  - Natural Language Traceable Output  |                       |\n",
    " +-------------------+-------------------+                       |\n",
    "                     |                                           |\n",
    "                     +---------------------+---------------------+\n",
    "                                           |\n",
    "                                           v\n",
    " +-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n",
    " |                     Phase 8: Evaluation, Visualization & Exports                  |\n",
    " |  - Similarity Heatmap, Spring Graph Layout, 2D PCA & TruncatedSVD                 |\n",
    " |  - Intra/Inter Similarity, Silhouette Analysis, (k, tau) Sensitivity Grid Search |\n",
    " |  - Academic Explainability Unit Tests & Multi-Format CSV/JSON Export               |\n",
    " +-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "### Algorithmic Distinctions & Academic Rigor\n",
    "1. **KNN Graph Clustering vs. K-Means**: Standard K-Means assumes isotropic, convex (spherical) clusters of equal variance in Euclidean space and forces every document into one of $K$ fixed centroids. In contrast, **KNN-based Graph Clustering** constructs a local topological manifold using cosine distances, builds a thresholded proximity graph, and partitions documents via connected components. This naturally discovers arbitrary cluster geometries, detects isolated outliers, and accurately captures real-world document relationships.\n",
    "2. **The Chaining Problem**: In connected component graph clustering, transitivity can link document $A$ to $B$ and $B$ to $C$, grouping $A$ and $C$ together even if their direct similarity is near zero. QuantumLens explicitly identifies and explains multi-hop paths to ensure full transparency.\n",
    "3. **Extractive TextRank vs. Generative Hallucination**: Rather than risking hallucination through generative language models, our primary summarization uses the graph-based **TextRank** algorithm, scoring sentences by eigenvector centrality and preserving verbatim sentences in chronological order."
   ]
