    "---\n",
    "## Phase 1: Multi-Modal User Document Ingestion & Validation\n",
    "\n",
    "To satisfy real-world engineering constraints, QuantumLens supports multi-modal document ingestion:\n",
    "1. **CSV Ingestion**: Tabular data containing Document IDs, Titles, Body Text, Sources, and Dates.\n",
    "2. **Direct Text Ingestion**: Programmatic Python lists or interactive dictionaries.\n",
    "3. **Multiple `.txt` File Ingestion**: Directory-based batch file readers.\n",
    "4. **Sample Benchmark Dataset**: 20 comprehensive quantum computing news articles covering hardware, error correction, algorithms, post-quantum cryptography, industrial use cases, and classical HPC baselines.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Validation Criteria & Edge Case Handling\n",
    "- **Schema Integrity**: Verifies presence of `doc_id`, `title`, and `text`.\n",
    "- **Missing / Null Values**: Automatically logs and removes corrupted records.\n",
    "- **Short Document Filter**: Rejects documents under a threshold (e.g. $< 10$ tokens) where statistical term frequency is unreliable.\n",
    "- **Deduplication Engine**: Uses cryptographic MD5 hashing of normalized text to identify exact duplicates and flags near-duplicates."
   ]
