    "---\n",
    "## Phase 3: Text Representation (TF-IDF Vector Space Modeling & Embeddings)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Primary Representation: TF-IDF with N-Grams and Sublinear Scaling\n",
    "Documents are mapped into a high-dimensional vector space $\\mathbb{R}^{|V|}$ using the Term Frequency-Inverse Document Frequency (TF-IDF) model. To capture both isolated keywords and multi-word technical concepts (e.g. *error correction*, *surface code*, *machine learning*), we configure unigrams and bigrams ($n \\in [1, 2]$).\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\text{TF-IDF}(t, d, D) = \\text{TF}_{\\text{sublinear}}(t, d) \\times \\text{IDF}(t, D)$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Where:\n",
    "- **Sublinear TF Scaling**: $\\text{TF}_{\\text{sublinear}}(t, d) = 1 + \\log(\\text{TF}(t, d))$ for $\\text{TF} > 0$ (dampens the excessive influence of repeated terms in longer articles).\n",
    "- **Smooth Inverse Document Frequency**: $\\text{IDF}(t, D) = \\log\\left(\\frac{1 + |D|}{1 + \\text{DF}(t, D)}\right) + 1$.\n",
    "- **L2 Unit Normalization**: Each vector is scaled such that $\\|\\mathbf{x}_d\\|_2 = 1$, ensuring that document length does not distort cosine similarity.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Optional Semantic Embedding Comparison\n",
    "When a pre-trained Sentence Transformer model (e.g. `all-MiniLM-L6-v2`) is available, QuantumLens can compute dense contextual embeddings and compare the semantic cosine similarity matrix against the sparse TF-IDF matrix. However, the system runs 100% offline using TF-IDF as the primary feature representation."
