    "---\n",
    "## Phase 9: Quantitative Evaluation & Sensitivity Experiments\n",
    "\n",
    "### Evaluation Methodology & Academic Criteria\n",
    "1. **Intra-Cluster Cohesion vs. Inter-Cluster Separation**:\n",
    "   - **Mean Intra-Cluster Similarity**: Average pairwise cosine similarity among documents within the same cluster (evaluates compactness).\n",
    "   - **Mean Inter-Cluster Similarity**: Average pairwise similarity between documents in different clusters (evaluates separation).\n",
    "2. **Silhouette Score**: Evaluates cluster cohesion against cluster separation: $s(i) = \\frac{b(i) - a(i)}{\\max(a(i), b(i))}$.\n",
    "   - *Academic Note*: Silhouette assumes convex clusters; in connected component graph clustering with non-linear manifolds, a modest silhouette score is expected and does not imply poor topological clustering.\n",
    "3. **Hyperparameter Grid Search ($k$ vs. $\\tau$)**:\n",
    "   - We systematically sweep neighborhood size $k \\in [2, 3, 4, 5]$ and similarity threshold $\\tau \\in [0.15, 0.20, 0.25, 0.30, 0.35, 0.40]$.\n",
    "   - We evaluate the resulting number of clusters, isolated documents, and the emergence of the **Chaining Problem** at low $\\tau$.\n",
    "4. **Academic Unit Tests for Explainability Verification**:\n",
    "   - Validates that reported shared keywords actually exist in feature sets.\n",
    "   - Validates that similarity scores match exact mathematical cosine distances.\n",
    "   - Verifies that every assigned document possesses an unbroken path in graph $G$."
   ]
